<title>USA: AMR Corp mulls aircraft replacements.</title>
<headline>AMR Corp mulls aircraft replacements.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMR Corp said Thursday that &quot;sometime fairly soon&quot; it is likely to pick a replacement for its MD-11s, the largest and longest range aircraft in its fleet.</p>
<p>The company also said it may acquire 757s to service its domestic routes and begin replacing its 727s with more modern, narrow-bodied planes.</p>
<p>It said however that capital spending will &quot;remain quite modest by historical standards, and our balance sheet should continue to improve.&quot;</p>
</text>
